enson</surname><given-names>CA</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><year>1997</year><article-title>Immunologic and virologic evaluation after influenza vaccination of HIV-1-infected patients.</article-title><source>Aids</source><volume>11</volume><fpage>1013</fpage><lpage>1021</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">9223736</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0002961-Douek1"><label>17</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Douek</surname><given-names>D</given-names></name></person-group><year>2007</year><article-title>HIV disease progression: immune activation, microbes, and a leaky gut.</article-title><source>Top HIV Med</source><volume>15</volume><fpage>114</fpage><lpage>117</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">17720995</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0002961-DyrholRiise1"><label>18</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Dyrhol-Riise</surname><given-names>AM</given-names></name><name><surname>Voltersvik</surname><given-names>P</given-names></name><name><surname>Olofsson</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Asjo</surname><given-names>B</given-names></name></person-group><year>1999</year><article-title>Activation of CD8 T cells normalizes and correlates with the level of infectious provirus in tonsils during highly active antiretroviral therapy in early HIV-1 infection.</article-title><source>Aids</source><volume>13</volume><fpage>2365</fpage><lpage>2376</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">10597778</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0002961-Sousa1"><label>19</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Sousa</surname><given-names>AE</given-names></name><name><surname>Carneiro</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Meier-Schellersheim</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Grossman</surname><given-names>Z</given-names></name><name><